    "alert_id": "ALERT_001",
    "title": "Rising creatinine and declining eGFR on TDF",
    "message": "Guidelines state that in patients on TDF who are admitted to hospital, it is important to check creatinine (eGFR) because intercurrent illnesses with dehydration or sepsis may cause renal deterioration. This patient is not admitted but shows a steady creatinine rise from 0.9 (2020) to 1.4 mg/dL (2026) with eGFR now 52 mL/min/1.73m². TDF is nephrotoxic and can cause proximal tubular damage leading to progressive renal impairment. Evidence for drug attribution: the gradual decline began after TDF initiation and TDF is a known nephrotoxin. Evidence against: the patient has no oedema or tubular dysfunction signs, and occasional ibuprofen use (2–3×/week) may also contribute to renal injury. Urinalysis showing protein 1+ is consistent with TDF nephrotoxicity.",
    "issue_type": "toxicity",
    "severity": "high",
    "recommended_action": "Urgent renal review. Consider substituting TDF with ABC or AZT given progressive creatinine rise and eGFR 52. Evaluate ibuprofen contribution and advise NSAID avoidance.",
    "citations": [
      {"page_number": 40, "chunk_id": "sahcs_adult_art_2024__sahcs_adult_art_2024__p40_c2"}
    ]
  },
  {
    "alert_id": "ALERT_002",
    "title": "No clinician assessment or plan documented",
    "message": "The clinician's assessment and plan section is blank for this visit. The patient has a significant creatinine trend (0.9 to 1.4 over 6 years) and declining eGFR (52 mL/min/1.73m²) that requires clinical action. Additionally, the patient takes ibuprofen 2–3 times weekly, which may compound renal risk alongside TDF. No orders, medicine changes, or monitoring plans were recorded. Guidelines indicate that patients on DTG-based ART require virological monitoring every 6 months if VL <50 for >1 year can extend to 12 monthly. The latest VL is suppressed (<50 copies/mL) and CD4 is 584, but renal monitoring and medication review are essential given the abnormal trend.",
    "issue_type": "plan_review",
    "severity": "high",
    "recommended_action": "Document assessment addressing creatinine trend and eGFR. Plan renal monitoring, review TDF continuation, counsel on ibuprofen avoidance, and schedule appropriate follow-up.",
